## Project-specific overlays

These conventions are specific to {ProjectName} and supplement (never contradict) the kit's handbooks.

### Project token

Channel addresses in this project use the prefix `{project}`. The shared event topic is `{project}.events`; scheduled-trigger channels are `{project}.{domain}.jobs`.

### Domain list

Active domains in this project:

- `{initial-domain}` — (one-line description of what this domain owns)

Add new domains here as the project grows. The Spectral validator loads this list to enforce `x-domain` values on AsyncAPI channels and Arazzo workflows.

### Role enum

The project's closed role enum is defined in [`api/specs/v1/common/enums.yaml#/Role`](api/specs/v1/common/enums.yaml). All `x-roles` declarations on secured endpoints must use values from this enum.

Starter shape (edit `enums.yaml` to add the roles your project actually needs):

- `Admin` — system administrator (full access)
- `Manager` — tenant-level manager
- `Customer` — end-user with self-service access
- `Authenticated` — pre-business-role flows (signup, invitation acceptance, etc.)

### AI access policy

The project's per-entity AI access tier assignments are documented in `api/docs/{ProjectName}-ai-access-policy.md` (copy from `<kit>/templates/ai-access-policy-template.md`). Every entity with `x-entity` must be assigned to a tier (0 = no access, 1 = read-only, 2 = collaborative, 3 = AI-owned). See `<kit>/handbooks/AI_Access_Policy_Framework.md` for tier semantics.

### Flow documentation

Each domain with async specifications has flow documentation under `api/docs/flows/{domain}/`. Flow docs are the primary resource for product managers and developers to understand how the system works end-to-end. Use Mermaid sequence diagrams for visual clarity.

